WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:04.740
Hello.

2
00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:11.510
I'm a professor of psychiatry at Seoul
National University Bundang Hospital.

3
00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:18.290
In this second episode, we will look at the
symptoms of mood disorders in this order: mood,

4
00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:22.870
emotional reactions, motivation, thinking and sensation.

5
00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:28.280
With a normal mood, even when
something good or bad happens,

6
00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:34.200
you feel good or bad for a few days, and
your mood stays within a certain range.

7
00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:36.380
In depression, however,

8
00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:43.500
you can feel depressed for weeks or months over
something that would make others depressed for a day,

9
00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:47.420
or become depressed for no particular reason.

10
00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:54.016
People describe feeling depressed in different ways.

11
00:00:54.036 --> 00:00:57.536
They say their mood is down, they feel
stifled, their chest feels blocked,

12
00:00:57.556 --> 00:00:59.260
everything is a bother,

13
00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:04.888
or they say they have become
sensitive, more irritable, or angrier.

14
00:01:04.908 --> 00:01:10.670
Exploding in anger over things others can put
up with is also a sign of a mood disorder.

15
00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:15.500
In mania or hypomania, the mood is elevated.

16
00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:20.560
It may last only a few days, or weeks, or even months.

17
00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:23.800
It doesn't happen only when something good happens.

18
00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:28.740
You may also become elevated while
struggling to overcome a difficulty.

19
00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:33.880
You may feel your depression has gone,
or that you have found yourself again,

20
00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:38.040
but people around you may see that you are not yourself.

21
00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:44.140
At first, work seems to go well, but in
most cases the state cannot be kept up.

22
00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:50.580
You become even more elevated, your moods
swing widely, or you fall into deep depression.

23
00:01:51.550 --> 00:01:56.070
In some people, depressive and
manic periods are clearly separated,

24
00:01:56.090 --> 00:01:59.210
and between them they feel comfortable.

25
00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:07.700
But in others, mild depression or elevation,
irritability and anxiety continue even in between.

26
00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:13.670
They may be mistaken for having a moody,
changeable or easily hurt personality.

27
00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:19.070
Some people have no severe depression but
a mild depression that lasts a long time,

28
00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:24.710
and they describe themselves as having
always been depressed since they were young.

29
00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:31.840
Along with the mood come emotional reactions
such as fear, timidity, worry and anxiety.

30
00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:37.480
It is hard to speak up in front of people,
and even small things make you anxious.

31
00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:42.360
Irritability and anger arise, so you may get very angry,

32
00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:46.220
or conflicts may arise over small matters.

33
00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:51.920
These emotional reactions can appear both when
you are depressed and when you are elevated.

34
00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:54.550
Motivation changes too.

35
00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:58.950
Things you usually enjoy become
dull, and everything is a bother,

36
00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:01.380
so you keep putting off what you have to do.

37
00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:08.060
As a result, students' grades drop, working
people's evaluations and relationships suffer,

38
00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:11.160
and parents may find child care hard.

39
00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:17.740
When you are elevated, on the other hand,
everything is fun and you are full of confidence.

40
00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:24.140
You make lots of plans and appointments, and
spending or risky investing may increase.

41
00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:30.240
These things are not done after careful
thought, so they often cause problems later,

42
00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:33.200
and you may become listless again.

43
00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:38.070
Your sleep, appetite and sexual desire also change,

44
00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:42.720
and the direction of the change
differs from person to person.

45
00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:48.320
When depressed, some people lose their
appetite, while others eat a lot.

46
00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:52.340
Some cannot sleep, while others only want to sleep.

47
00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:57.220
When elevated, you may not feel
hungry even if you don't eat,

48
00:03:57.240 --> 00:04:01.290
and you may not feel tired even if you don't sleep.

49
00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:04.140
Thinking changes too.

50
00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:11.000
Your thinking slows down and your head goes blank,
so nothing stays in your mind when you read,

51
00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:13.820
and you may not follow conversations well.

52
00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:21.420
At other times your thinking speeds up and thoughts
follow one after another, so ideas overflow,

53
00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:23.590
and you talk and write more.

54
00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:27.950
Negative thoughts may chain
together into extreme thoughts,

55
00:04:27.970 --> 00:04:31.690
or you may be full of confidence without any basis.

56
00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:36.860
When thinking goes too far,
ideas of reference may appear,

57
00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:42.780
linking events unrelated to you with
yourself, and it can even reach delusions.

58
00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:48.080
Examples are thinking that people
recognize you, that you are being watched,

59
00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:53.600
that others know your thoughts, or that
you have become an important person.

60
00:04:53.820 --> 00:05:00.460
When these symptoms are severe, it can sometimes
be hard to tell them apart from schizophrenia.

61
00:05:01.430 --> 00:05:03.210
Sensation also changes.

62
00:05:03.230 --> 00:05:08.070
Pain you already had may get worse,
and you may have chest tightness,

63
00:05:08.090 --> 00:05:13.290
a burning feeling like hwabyung, an
anger-related illness, dizziness,

64
00:05:13.310 --> 00:05:15.830
hyperventilation or panic attacks.

65
00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:21.850
When the state is severe, hallucinations,
such as hearing voices or seeing things,

66
00:05:21.870 --> 00:05:24.250
may appear together with delusions.

67
00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:30.960
Hypomania is short and causes little trouble
in daily life, so it is hard to remember.

68
00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:38.380
That is why the Guide includes the Korean
Bipolar Spectrum Diagnostic Scale, K-BSDS.

69
00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:44.080
Read the 19 sentences and mark O if
one is similar to you, or X if not.

70
00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:46.040
Each O is 1 point.

71
00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:51.900
Then choose how much the whole description
is like you, and add that score.

72
00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:57.640
Completely like me is 6 points, quite
like me is 4, like me in some ways is 2,

73
00:05:57.660 --> 00:06:00.240
and not at all like me is 0.

74
00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:06.220
A total of 6 or less means the likelihood
of bipolar disorder is very low.

75
00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:12.020
7 to 12 is low, 13 to 19 is possible,
and 20 or more is very high.

76
00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:17.180
However, a simple questionnaire
cannot replace a doctor's diagnosis.

77
00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:22.040
Please talk through the result
with your doctor at your visit.

78
00:06:23.010 --> 00:06:28.990
Mood disorders affect not only mood but
also emotional reactions, motivation,

79
00:06:29.010 --> 00:06:30.490
thinking and sensation.

80
00:06:30.510 --> 00:06:36.650
The symptoms are so varied that they are
easily brushed off as personality or stress.

81
00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:37.550
Next time,

82
00:06:37.570 --> 00:06:45.550
we will use graphs to look at how mood moves over
time and at the different courses of mood disorders.

83
00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:46.840
Thank you.
